# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trivy ignore file - POLICY: no active ignores.
#
# This file exists so that the policy is explicit and reviewable, not so that
# findings can be silenced. An empty ignore list is intentional.
#
# Rules for adding an entry (all three are mandatory):
#   1. The CVE has NO fixed version available, or the vulnerable code path is
#      provably unreachable in this application.
#   2. A comment above the entry records: CVE id, why it is not exploitable
#      here, the owner, and a review-by date.
#   3. The entry is referenced in a pull request description and re-reviewed
#      at the stated date.
#
# Example of an ACCEPTABLE entry (format only - not active):
#   # CVE-2099-00000 - Go stdlib, no fix published. Only reachable via a CLI
#   # flag this service never exposes. Owner: roushan. Review by: 2026-12-31.
#   CVE-2099-00000
#
# Note: the CI pipeline also passes --ignore-unfixed, which skips findings that
# have no available fix. That is a documented, repo-wide policy decision, not a
# per-finding suppression, and it is visible in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
